{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-107269","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-172980","text":"Runefort Protocol — v0.1"}]},{"id":"blk-107270","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-172981","marks":["bold"],"text":"A layout protocol for living, file-backed, tile-grid web apps."}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107272","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-172982","marks":["bold"],"text":"Part of the [&] Protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-172983","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-172984","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/ECOSYSTEM.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem overview"},{"id":"spn-172985","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-172986","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/THREE_PROTOCOL_STACK.md"}],"text":"Three-protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-172987","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-172988","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/STACK_COMPLETION.md"}],"text":"Stack status"}]}],"id":"blk-107271","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-107273","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-172989","text":"Status: draft v0.1 Owner: runefort.com Date: 2026-04-25 Position: protocol-level. Independent of [&], PULSE, PRISM. May be used by them; does not require them."}]},{"id":"blk-107274","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-172990","marks":["bold"],"text":"Related documents:"}]},{"id":"blk-107275","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107277","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-172991","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/docs/spec/runefort.core.md"}],"text":"@runefort/core — Reference Web Component Framework v0.1"}]}],"id":"blk-107276","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107279","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-172992","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/docs/spec/runefort.dsl.md"}],"text":".rune DSL — v0.1"}]}],"id":"blk-107278","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107281","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-172993","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-BUILD-ORDER.md"}],"text":"Interactive Layer — Build Order"}]}],"id":"blk-107280","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107283","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-172994","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-1_BYOK.md"}],"text":"RFort-1 — BYOK Modal + OpenRouter Key Storage"}]}],"id":"blk-107282","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107285","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-172995","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-2_MCP.md"}],"text":"RFort-2 — MCP Proxy + Client + Connection Panel"}]}],"id":"blk-107284","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107287","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-172996","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-3_CHAT.md"}],"text":"RFort-3 — Chat Panel with Fort-Aware Navigation"}]}],"id":"blk-107286","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107289","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-172997","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-4_TOKENFLOWS.md"}],"text":"RFort-4 — Token Flow Animations on Edges"}]}],"id":"blk-107288","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107291","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-172998","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-5_REPO_IMPORT.md"}],"text":"RFort-5 — Repo Import → Fort Generator"}]}],"id":"blk-107290","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107293","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-172999","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-6_WORKSPACES.md"}],"text":"RFort-6 — Workspace Switcher + Supabase Persistence"}]}],"id":"blk-107292","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107294","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173000","text":"0. What this is, in one paragraph"}]},{"id":"blk-107295","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173001","text":"Runefort is a small declarative protocol for describing a "},{"id":"spn-173002","marks":["bold"],"text":"tiled, file-backed UI layout"},{"id":"spn-173003","text":". You declare "},{"id":"spn-173004","marks":["italic"],"text":"rooms"},{"id":"spn-173005","text":" (tiles), "},{"id":"spn-173006","marks":["italic"],"text":"claims"},{"id":"spn-173007","text":" (file-system regions each room owns), "},{"id":"spn-173008","marks":["italic"],"text":"neighbors"},{"id":"spn-173009","text":" (adjacency for navigation), and "},{"id":"spn-173010","marks":["italic"],"text":"state bindings"},{"id":"spn-173011","text":" (how live state colors a tile). A conformant renderer compiles the declaration to a CSS grid, surfaces each claim's content for inline viewing or editing, and overlays live state. The protocol is the contract between the declaration and the renderer. Nothing more."}]},{"id":"blk-107296","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173012","text":"It is not a workforce platform. It is not a supervisor framework. It is not a graph visualization library. It is the "},{"id":"spn-173013","marks":["bold"],"text":"layout language"},{"id":"spn-173014","text":" that those things can be built with."}]},{"id":"blk-107297","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173015","text":"1. Why a protocol (not a library)"}]},{"id":"blk-107298","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107300","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173016","marks":["bold"],"text":"Renderer-portable."},{"id":"spn-173017","text":" The same "},{"id":"spn-173018","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-173019","text":" should render in Elixir/Phoenix, TypeScript/React, or static HTML. The protocol is the only thing they share."}]}],"id":"blk-107299","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107302","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173020","marks":["bold"],"text":"Diffable."},{"id":"spn-173021","text":" Layouts live in version control as text. Reviews become readable. SVG graph layouts cannot do this."}]}],"id":"blk-107301","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107304","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173022","marks":["bold"],"text":"Extensible by composition."},{"id":"spn-173023","text":" Apps add "},{"id":"spn-173024","marks":["italic"],"text":"vocabularies"},{"id":"spn-173025","text":" (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-173026","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor"},{"id":"spn-173027","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173028","marks":["code"],"text":"dashboard"},{"id":"spn-173029","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173030","marks":["code"],"text":"wiki-page"},{"id":"spn-173031","text":") on top of the core primitives. The protocol does not know about supervisors."}]}],"id":"blk-107303","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107306","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173032","marks":["bold"],"text":"No runtime layout engine required."},{"id":"spn-173033","text":" All layout is compile-time deterministic. No d3, no dagre, no jitter."}]}],"id":"blk-107305","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107307","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173034","text":"2. Core primitives"}]},{"id":"blk-107308","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173035","text":"Four primitives. That is the entire vocabulary."}]},{"id":"blk-107309","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173036","text":"2.1 Room"}]},{"id":"blk-107310","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173037","text":"A room is a tile in the grid. It has an id, a position, a size, and arbitrary metadata."}]},{"id":"blk-107311","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"id\": \"memory\",\n  \"position\": [0, 0],\n  \"size\": [3, 2],\n  \"label\": \"memory.ex\",\n  \"meta\": {}\n}"},{"id":"blk-107312","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173038","marks":["code"],"text":"position"},{"id":"spn-173039","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-173040","marks":["code"],"text":"size"},{"id":"spn-173041","text":" are integer cell coordinates in a CSS grid. "},{"id":"spn-173042","marks":["code"],"text":"[0,0]"},{"id":"spn-173043","text":" is top-left. "},{"id":"spn-173044","marks":["code"],"text":"size: [3,2]"},{"id":"spn-173045","text":" means 3 columns wide, 2 rows tall. The renderer is free to choose the cell pixel size; the protocol only specifies cell counts."}]},{"id":"blk-107313","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173046","text":"2.2 Claim"}]},{"id":"blk-107314","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173047","text":"A claim is a file-system region a room \"owns.\" A renderer uses claims to (a) list which files belong to a room and (b) surface those files inline — either as a viewer or an editor — when the user activates the room. Optional behaviors include generating external-editor handoff URLs ("},{"id":"spn-173048","marks":["code"],"text":"vscode://"},{"id":"spn-173049","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173050","marks":["code"],"text":"cursor://"},{"id":"spn-173051","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173052","marks":["code"],"text":"zed://"},{"id":"spn-173053","text":") for users who prefer their own tools."}]},{"id":"blk-107315","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"room\": \"memory\",\n  \"pattern\": \"lib/my_app/memory/**/*.ex\",\n  \"anchor\": \"lib/my_app/forge/memory.ex#L24\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-107316","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173054","marks":["code"],"text":"pattern"},{"id":"spn-173055","text":" is a glob. "},{"id":"spn-173056","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-173057","text":" is the canonical file the room represents (the one a click on the tile opens)."}]},{"id":"blk-107317","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173058","text":"2.3 Neighbor"}]},{"id":"blk-107318","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173059","text":"A neighbor declares an adjacency between two rooms. Neighbors drive keyboard navigation ("},{"id":"spn-173060","marks":["code"],"text":"h/j/k/l"},{"id":"spn-173061","text":"), focus order, and may be rendered as connecting lines."}]},{"id":"blk-107319","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"from\": \"memory\", \"to\": \"deploy\", \"kind\": \"adjacent\" }"},{"id":"blk-107320","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173062","marks":["code"],"text":"kind"},{"id":"spn-173063","text":" is one of: "},{"id":"spn-173064","marks":["code"],"text":"adjacent"},{"id":"spn-173065","text":" (touching), "},{"id":"spn-173066","marks":["code"],"text":"linked"},{"id":"spn-173067","text":" (logical link, may not be touching), "},{"id":"spn-173068","marks":["code"],"text":"nested"},{"id":"spn-173069","text":" (one contains the other)."}]},{"id":"blk-107321","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173070","text":"2.4 State binding"}]},{"id":"blk-107322","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173071","text":"A state binding tells the renderer how to color a room based on a runtime signal. The protocol defines the "},{"id":"spn-173072","marks":["italic"],"text":"binding"},{"id":"spn-173073","text":", not the signal source — signals are pushed to the renderer over whatever transport the host app provides (WebSocket, SSE, polling, static)."}]},{"id":"blk-107323","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"room\": \"memory\",\n  \"signal\": \"kappa\",\n  \"thresholds\": [\n    { \"if\": \"< 0.3\", \"class\": \"cold\" },\n    { \"if\": \"< 0.6\", \"class\": \"warm\" },\n    { \"if\": \">= 0.6\", \"class\": \"hot\" }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-107324","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173074","marks":["code"],"text":"class"},{"id":"spn-173075","text":" is a token the renderer maps to CSS. The protocol reserves five canonical classes: "},{"id":"spn-173076","marks":["code"],"text":"cold"},{"id":"spn-173077","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173078","marks":["code"],"text":"warm"},{"id":"spn-173079","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173080","marks":["code"],"text":"hot"},{"id":"spn-173081","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173082","marks":["code"],"text":"fault"},{"id":"spn-173083","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173084","marks":["code"],"text":"idle"},{"id":"spn-173085","text":". Apps may add custom classes — renderers should ignore unknown classes gracefully (treat as "},{"id":"spn-173086","marks":["code"],"text":"cold"},{"id":"spn-173087","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-107325","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173088","text":"3. Document shape"}]},{"id":"blk-107326","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173089","text":"A complete "},{"id":"spn-173090","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-173091","text":" is just an object containing arrays of the four primitives, plus header metadata."}]},{"id":"blk-107327","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"runefort\": \"0.1\",\n  \"title\": \"my_app forge floor\",\n  \"grid\": { \"columns\": 6, \"rows\": 4 },\n  \"rooms\": [ ... ],\n  \"claims\": [ ... ],\n  \"neighbors\": [ ... ],\n  \"state_bindings\": [ ... ],\n  \"vocabulary\": \"core\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-107328","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173092","marks":["code"],"text":"grid.columns"},{"id":"spn-173093","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-173094","marks":["code"],"text":"grid.rows"},{"id":"spn-173095","text":" are the total grid dimensions. "},{"id":"spn-173096","marks":["code"],"text":"vocabulary"},{"id":"spn-173097","text":" is the name of the extension vocabulary in use; "},{"id":"spn-173098","marks":["code"],"text":"\"core\""},{"id":"spn-173099","text":" means no extensions."}]},{"id":"blk-107329","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173100","text":"4. The DSL surface (host-language sugar)"}]},{"id":"blk-107330","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173101","text":"Hosts may expose a DSL that compiles to the JSON above. The DSL is "},{"id":"spn-173102","marks":["bold"],"text":"not normative"},{"id":"spn-173103","text":" — only the JSON is. A reference Elixir DSL:"}]},{"id":"blk-107331","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"defmodule MyApp.Floor do\n  use Runefort.Layout, columns: 6, rows: 4\n\n  room :memory,\n    at: {0, 0}, size: {3, 2},\n    claims: ~r{lib/my_app/memory/},\n    anchor: \"lib/my_app/forge/memory.ex:24\"\n\n  room :deploy,\n    at: {3, 0}, size: {3, 2},\n    claims: ~r{lib/my_app/deploy/}\n\n  neighbors :memory => :deploy\n\n  bind :memory, signal: :kappa,\n    cold: \"< 0.3\", warm: \"< 0.6\", hot: \">= 0.6\"\nend"},{"id":"blk-107332","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173104","text":"A reference TypeScript DSL:"}]},{"id":"blk-107333","kind":"code","language":"ts","text":"const floor = layout({ columns: 6, rows: 4 }, [\n  room(\"memory\", { at: [0,0], size: [3,2], claims: \"lib/my_app/memory/**\" }),\n  room(\"deploy\", { at: [3,0], size: [3,2], claims: \"lib/my_app/deploy/**\" }),\n  neighbor(\"memory\", \"deploy\"),\n  bind(\"memory\", \"kappa\", { cold: \"< 0.3\", warm: \"< 0.6\", hot: \">= 0.6\" }),\n]);"},{"id":"blk-107334","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173105","text":"Both compile to the same JSON. Either is conformant. Neither is privileged."}]},{"id":"blk-107335","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173106","text":"5. Renderer contract"}]},{"id":"blk-107336","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173107","text":"A conformant renderer MUST:"}]},{"id":"blk-107337","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107339","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173108","marks":["bold"],"text":"Layout."},{"id":"spn-173109","text":" Render rooms in a CSS grid (or visually equivalent) using each room's "},{"id":"spn-173110","marks":["code"],"text":"position"},{"id":"spn-173111","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-173112","marks":["code"],"text":"size"},{"id":"spn-173113","text":". The grid MUST be deterministic — given the same JSON, the rendered DOM order MUST be stable."}]}],"id":"blk-107338","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107341","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173114","marks":["bold"],"text":"Anchors."},{"id":"spn-173115","text":" Resolve each room's "},{"id":"spn-173116","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-173117","text":" to its content (the file or content region the room represents). Activating a tile MUST surface that content — by default, inline within the host page (viewer or editor). Renderers MAY additionally offer an external-editor handoff URL as a secondary action, but inline surfacing is the canonical behavior."}]}],"id":"blk-107340","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107343","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173118","marks":["bold"],"text":"State classes."},{"id":"spn-173119","text":" Apply CSS classes from "},{"id":"spn-173120","marks":["code"],"text":"state_bindings"},{"id":"spn-173121","text":" to each room's root element. Class names MUST be predictable: "},{"id":"spn-173122","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort-state-cold"},{"id":"spn-173123","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173124","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort-state-hot"},{"id":"spn-173125","text":", etc."}]}],"id":"blk-107342","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107345","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173126","marks":["bold"],"text":"Accessibility."},{"id":"spn-173127","text":" Each room MUST be focusable (keyboard) and have a stable accessible name (the room's "},{"id":"spn-173128","marks":["code"],"text":"label"},{"id":"spn-173129","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-173130","marks":["code"],"text":"id"},{"id":"spn-173131","text":")."}]}],"id":"blk-107344","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107347","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173132","marks":["bold"],"text":"Neighbor navigation."},{"id":"spn-173133","text":" Arrow keys (or "},{"id":"spn-173134","marks":["code"],"text":"h/j/k/l"},{"id":"spn-173135","text":") MUST move focus along "},{"id":"spn-173136","marks":["code"],"text":"neighbor"},{"id":"spn-173137","text":" edges. Renderers MAY also expose mouse navigation; keyboard support is required."}]}],"id":"blk-107346","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-107348","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173138","text":"A conformant renderer SHOULD:"}]},{"id":"blk-107349","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107351","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173139","text":"Provide an inline editor (not just a read-only viewer) for the focused room's "},{"id":"spn-173140","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-173141","text":" when the host environment supports text editing."}]}],"id":"blk-107350","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107353","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173142","text":"Highlight neighbor adjacencies on hover/focus."}]}],"id":"blk-107352","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107355","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173143","text":"Re-render on signal change without full reload."}]}],"id":"blk-107354","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107356","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173144","text":"A conformant renderer MAY:"}]},{"id":"blk-107357","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107359","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173145","text":"Add domain-specific vocabularies (see §6)."}]}],"id":"blk-107358","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107361","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173146","text":"Display additional metadata from "},{"id":"spn-173147","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-173148","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-107360","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107363","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173149","text":"Animate state class transitions."}]}],"id":"blk-107362","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107365","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173150","text":"Offer external-editor handoff URLs ("},{"id":"spn-173151","marks":["code"],"text":"vscode://"},{"id":"spn-173152","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173153","marks":["code"],"text":"cursor://"},{"id":"spn-173154","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173155","marks":["code"],"text":"zed://"},{"id":"spn-173156","text":") as a secondary action for users who prefer their own tools. Renderers that run outside the browser (e.g. static-site generators, server-rendered HTML with no JS) MAY treat handoff as their primary surfacing strategy and still claim conformance."}]}],"id":"blk-107364","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107366","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173157","text":"6. Vocabularies (extension points)"}]},{"id":"blk-107367","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173158","text":"The protocol's core knows nothing about supervisors, dashboards, or wikis. Apps declare a "},{"id":"spn-173159","marks":["italic"],"text":"vocabulary"},{"id":"spn-173160","text":" — a named bundle of extra fields on "},{"id":"spn-173161","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-173162","text":", extra signals, and extra state classes."}]},{"id":"blk-107368","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"runefort\": \"0.1\",\n  \"vocabulary\": \"supervisor-floor.v1\",\n  \"rooms\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"memory\",\n      \"position\": [0,0], \"size\": [3,2],\n      \"meta\": {\n        \"supervisor\": {\n          \"autonomy\": \"advise\",\n          \"uptime_seconds\": 957840,\n          \"last_action\": \"consolidated 47 nodes\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-107369","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173163","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-173164","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-173165","text":" vocabulary defines what "},{"id":"spn-173166","marks":["code"],"text":"meta.supervisor"},{"id":"spn-173167","text":" contains. A renderer that doesn't know "},{"id":"spn-173168","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-173169","text":" MUST still render the layout correctly — it just won't display the supervisor-specific overlay. "},{"id":"spn-173170","marks":["bold"],"text":"Vocabulary unknown = degrade, don't fail."}]},{"id":"blk-107370","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173171","text":"Reserved vocabularies (managed by the protocol authors):"}]},{"id":"blk-107371","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107373","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173172","marks":["code"],"text":"core"},{"id":"spn-173173","text":" — the four primitives, no extensions."}]}],"id":"blk-107372","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107375","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173174","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-173175","text":" — for [&]/Runefort supervisor workforce apps."}]}],"id":"blk-107374","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107377","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173176","marks":["code"],"text":"codebase-atlas.v1"},{"id":"spn-173177","text":" — for repository visualization apps."}]}],"id":"blk-107376","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107379","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173178","marks":["code"],"text":"dashboard-grid.v1"},{"id":"spn-173179","text":" — for metric/observability tile dashboards."}]}],"id":"blk-107378","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107380","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173180","text":"Custom vocabularies are namespaced freely ("},{"id":"spn-173181","marks":["code"],"text":"com.example.my-vocab.v1"},{"id":"spn-173182","text":"). The protocol does not require registration."}]},{"id":"blk-107381","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173183","text":"7. Non-goals"}]},{"id":"blk-107382","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173184","text":"Explicit, so the protocol stays small:"}]},{"id":"blk-107383","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107385","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173185","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a graph visualization protocol."},{"id":"spn-173186","text":" Force-directed layouts, dagre, hierarchies — out of scope. Runefort is grids only. If you need a graph, use a graph tool."}]}],"id":"blk-107384","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107387","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173187","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a state-management protocol."},{"id":"spn-173188","text":" How signals are computed, where they live, how they're transported — host's problem."}]}],"id":"blk-107386","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107389","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173189","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a workforce / supervision framework."},{"id":"spn-173190","text":" That's a "},{"id":"spn-173191","marks":["italic"],"text":"vocabulary"},{"id":"spn-173192","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-173193","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-173194","text":"), built on top."}]}],"id":"blk-107388","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107391","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173195","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a presentation framework."},{"id":"spn-173196","text":" No theming spec, no animation spec. CSS is the renderer's job."}]}],"id":"blk-107390","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107393","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173197","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not coupled to [&], PULSE, or PRISM."},{"id":"spn-173198","text":" A "},{"id":"spn-173199","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-173200","text":" describing a recipe app is fully conformant."}]}],"id":"blk-107392","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107394","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173201","text":"8. Versioning"}]},{"id":"blk-107395","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173202","text":"Semver for the protocol itself. The top-level "},{"id":"spn-173203","marks":["code"],"text":"\"runefort\": \"0.1\""},{"id":"spn-173204","text":" field is the protocol version, NOT the renderer version."}]},{"id":"blk-107396","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107398","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173205","marks":["bold"],"text":"Major bump"},{"id":"spn-173206","text":" = breaking JSON shape change."}]}],"id":"blk-107397","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107400","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173207","marks":["bold"],"text":"Minor bump"},{"id":"spn-173208","text":" = additive (new optional fields, new reserved vocabularies, new state classes)."}]}],"id":"blk-107399","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107402","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173209","marks":["bold"],"text":"Patch"},{"id":"spn-173210","text":" = clarification only, no behavior change."}]}],"id":"blk-107401","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107403","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173211","text":"A renderer MUST refuse documents with a major version it does not support. A renderer SHOULD render documents with a higher minor version, ignoring fields it does not recognize."}]},{"id":"blk-107404","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173212","text":"9. Reference framework — "},{"id":"spn-173213","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"}]},{"id":"blk-107405","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173214","text":"The canonical browser-side reference implementation is "},{"id":"spn-173215","marks":["bold"],"text":"`@runefort/core`"},{"id":"spn-173216","text":": a small set of Web Components ("},{"id":"spn-173217","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-floor>"},{"id":"spn-173218","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173219","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-room>"},{"id":"spn-173220","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173221","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-claim>"},{"id":"spn-173222","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173223","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-link>"},{"id":"spn-173224","text":") implementing this protocol with no framework dependency. ~5KB minified target. Specified in "},{"id":"spn-173225","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.core.md"},{"id":"spn-173226","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-107406","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173227","text":"Why a reference framework, not just a renderer:"}]},{"id":"blk-107407","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107409","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173228","marks":["bold"],"text":"Zero-build adoption."},{"id":"spn-173229","text":" Drop one "},{"id":"spn-173230","marks":["code"],"text":"<script type=\"module\">"},{"id":"spn-173231","text":" tag into any HTML page and the protocol is rendered. No bundler, no npm, no framework."}]}],"id":"blk-107408","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107411","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173232","marks":["bold"],"text":"Universal embedding."},{"id":"spn-173233","text":" Custom Elements work inside React, Vue, Svelte, Solid, Lit, Astro, Phoenix LiveView, Rails view templates, plain HTML. The framework adapters are ~1KB each, not full reimplementations."}]}],"id":"blk-107410","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107413","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173234","marks":["bold"],"text":"Single reactivity story."},{"id":"spn-173235","text":" Property setters on "},{"id":"spn-173236","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-floor>"},{"id":"spn-173237","text":" push signal updates; rooms recompute their state class. No virtual DOM, no opinionated state library — composes with whatever the host app already uses."}]}],"id":"blk-107412","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107414","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173238","text":"Conformant alternatives may exist. "},{"id":"spn-173239","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"},{"id":"spn-173240","text":" is the reference, not the only option. A pure-Phoenix-LiveView renderer or a server-rendered static-HTML emitter are both valid conformant implementations."}]},{"id":"blk-107415","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173241","text":"9.1 Authoring surfaces"}]},{"id":"blk-107416","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173242","text":"The same protocol is reachable through three authoring surfaces, all equivalent and all round-trippable:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-107418","spans":[{"id":"spn-173243","text":"Surface"}]},{"id":"blk-107419","spans":[{"id":"spn-173244","text":"Format"}]},{"id":"blk-107420","spans":[{"id":"spn-173245","text":"Use case"}]}],"id":"blk-107417","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-107421","spans":[{"id":"spn-173246","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"}]},{"id":"blk-107422","spans":[{"id":"spn-173247","text":"JSON"}]},{"id":"blk-107423","spans":[{"id":"spn-173248","text":"Programmatic generation, tooling integration, canonical persistence"}]}],[{"id":"blk-107424","spans":[{"id":"spn-173249","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-*>"},{"id":"spn-173250","text":" HTML"}]},{"id":"blk-107425","spans":[{"id":"spn-173251","text":"Custom Elements"}]},{"id":"blk-107426","spans":[{"id":"spn-173252","text":"Hand-written pages, embedding inside existing apps"}]}],[{"id":"blk-107427","spans":[{"id":"spn-173253","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-173254","text":" DSL"}]},{"id":"blk-107428","spans":[{"id":"spn-173255","text":"Curly-brace declarative"}]},{"id":"blk-107429","spans":[{"id":"spn-173256","text":"Hand-authored layouts, version control reviewability"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-107430","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173257","text":"The DSL is specified in "},{"id":"spn-173258","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.dsl.md"},{"id":"spn-173259","text":". The CLI converts losslessly between all three."}]},{"id":"blk-107431","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173260","text":"9.2 Planned tree"}]},{"id":"blk-107432","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"runefort/\n  spec/\n    runefort.protocol.md       ← this document\n    runefort.core.md           ← @runefort/core web component spec\n    runefort.dsl.md            ← .rune DSL spec\n    schema.json                ← JSON schema for runefort.json\n  packages/\n    core/                      ← @runefort/core (web components, target ≤5KB)\n    cli/                       ← runefort CLI (compile/fmt/to-rune)\n    react/                     ← @runefort/react adapter (~1KB)\n    vue/                       ← @runefort/vue adapter\n    svelte/                    ← @runefort/svelte adapter\n    liveview/                  ← @runefort/liveview adapter\n  examples/\n    no-framework/              ← raw HTML, proves \"runs anywhere\"\n    supervisor-floor/          ← the [&] use case, proves supervisor-floor.v1\n    codebase-atlas/            ← non-[&], proves genericity\n    dashboard-grid/            ← non-[&], proves genericity"},{"id":"blk-107433","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173261","text":"Two non-[&] examples are required before we cut v0.1 final. Otherwise we're an [&] dashboard with a spec attached."}]},{"id":"blk-107434","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173262","text":"9.3 Build order (v0.1)"}]},{"id":"blk-107435","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107437","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173263","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"},{"id":"spn-173264","text":" — the four web components + "},{"id":"spn-173265","marks":["code"],"text":"mount(json)"},{"id":"spn-173266","text":". Smallest meaningful artifact."}]}],"id":"blk-107436","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107439","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173267","text":"Playground at runefort.com — live "},{"id":"spn-173268","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-173269","text":" editor → rendered floor. The shareable demo."}]}],"id":"blk-107438","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107441","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173270","text":"CLI compile path — "},{"id":"spn-173271","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-173272","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-173273","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-173274","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-173275","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-173276","text":" → static HTML."}]}],"id":"blk-107440","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107443","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173277","text":"Adapters — React, then LiveView, then others as demand appears."}]}],"id":"blk-107442","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-107444","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173278","text":"Adapters wait until non-zero users exist. Shipping all adapters before having users is the wrong direction of optimization."}]},{"id":"blk-107445","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173279","text":"10. Relationship to the [&] stack"}]},{"id":"blk-107446","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173280","text":"Runefort is "},{"id":"spn-173281","marks":["bold"],"text":"independent of"},{"id":"spn-173282","text":" [&]. It does not import, depend on, or require any [&] protocol. However:"}]},{"id":"blk-107447","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107449","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173283","marks":["code"],"text":"[&]"},{"id":"spn-173284","text":" capability descriptors MAY be embedded in "},{"id":"spn-173285","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-173286","text":" under "},{"id":"spn-173287","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-173288","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-107448","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107451","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173289","text":"PULSE manifest phases MAY drive room generation in tooling that bridges PULSE → Runefort."}]}],"id":"blk-107450","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107453","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173290","text":"PRISM scores MAY be a signal source for state bindings."}]}],"id":"blk-107452","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107454","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173291","text":"These are "},{"id":"spn-173292","marks":["italic"],"text":"integration patterns"},{"id":"spn-173293","text":", not protocol requirements. A Runefort layout that knows nothing about [&] is fully conformant."}]},{"id":"blk-107455","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173294","text":"11. Open questions for v0.2"}]},{"id":"blk-107456","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107458","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173295","marks":["bold"],"text":"Nesting."},{"id":"spn-173296","text":" A room inside a room (zoomable). Worth adding to core, or push to a vocabulary?"}]}],"id":"blk-107457","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107460","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173297","marks":["bold"],"text":"Streaming layout edits."},{"id":"spn-173298","text":" Today the JSON is whole-document. Should there be a patch format?"}]}],"id":"blk-107459","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107462","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173299","marks":["bold"],"text":"Manifest discovery."},{"id":"spn-173300","text":" Does a renderer auto-discover "},{"id":"spn-173301","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-173302","text":" in a repo, or is the path always provided?"}]}],"id":"blk-107461","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107464","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173303","marks":["bold"],"text":"Multiple anchors per room."},{"id":"spn-173304","text":" Today one anchor. Real codebases have N files per logical region."}]}],"id":"blk-107463","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107465","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173305","text":"These are explicitly deferred. v0.1 ships with the four primitives and nothing else."}]},{"id":"blk-107466","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173306","marks":["italic"],"text":"This spec is the contract. Everything in `runefort.com/docs/spec/README.md` (the spatial-cognition / dark-factory spec) is now reframed as the `supervisor-floor.v1` vocabulary plus the `runefort.dark_factory` reference application — both built on top of this protocol."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierap3kpgm2af7jzooiveab5dku5cf3bv2tnnpcamj3c7c2dqdi34fra","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}